{
  "description": "std-agent-assistant — an in-app assistant that operates the running app for the signed-in user. One request flows down a chain of std agent atoms on the bus: the conversation (std-agent-session) SENDs → CONVERSE → std-agent-context bounds it → std-agent-memory adds what it recalls → std-agent-tool-loop answers it through `call-service llm call-tools`, firing only the inputs and reading only the entities the `tools` allowlist names, as the signed-in user → REPLIED goes back to the conversation, to memory (remembered) and to std-agent-trace (the run record). Import the orbital and supply the allowlist: `orbital Assistant = Agent.orbitals.AgentAssistantOrbital { config { tools: [{ event: TaskOrbital.TaskPersistor.DO_CREATE }, { read: Task }], instructions: \"…\" } }`. The conversation, memory and run records live in AgentRecordsOrbital; retarget them onto your own owner-scoped entities (`ownerId` a relation to your [identity] roster, with @read/@create) with `entities { AgentMessage: …, AgentMemory: …, AgentRun: … }`.",
